5. `<=0` GUARD. No validation clamps GuardrailConfig fields on load (only
   the form's clampedFloatField applies min/max on submit), so a
   hand-edited whatif.json could set e.g. CeilingRisePct=0. That yields
   RaiseTrigger = Baseline*(1+0/100) = Baseline > 0 for any normal positive
   portfolio, so the <=0 guard does not spuriously fire from realistic
   percentage edge cases; it functions as documented, catching only "no
   base projection yet" / zero-value-struct cases. Hiding both lines
   together (rather than one) is a reasonable, spec-consistent choice
   (SPEC.md GV4: "hidden ... otherwise", no per-line partial-hide
   requirement). Not a functional defect.

